[{"id":"NEWDER-001","sourceQ":721,"stem":"A blue monochrome identified as International Klein Blue most directly points to which artist?","choices":["Yves Klein","Mark Rothko","Barnett Newman","Piero Manzoni","Jean Tinguely"],"answer":"Yves Klein","why":"Klein developed and used International Klein Blue in his monochromes.","label":"A blue monochrome identified as International Klein Blue most directly p","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-002","sourceQ":722,"stem":"A scholar interprets the symbolic meanings of figures in a Renaissance painting. Which approach is being used?","choices":["Iconology","Formal analysis","Conservation science","Stratigraphy","Dendrochronology"],"answer":"Iconology","why":"Iconology interprets symbolic meaning rather than just technique or dating.","label":"A scholar interprets the symbolic meanings of figures in a Renaissance p","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-003","sourceQ":723,"stem":"What other name identifies architect Charles-Édouard Jeanneret?","choices":["Le Corbusier","Gio Ponti","Alvar Aalto","Walter Gropius","Ludwig Mies van der Rohe"],"answer":"Le Corbusier","why":"Jeanneret adopted the professional name Le Corbusier.","label":"What other name identifies architect Charles-Édouard Jeanneret","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-004","sourceQ":724,"stem":"Which approach to a plain building is most consistent with Adolf Loos's argument about ornament?","choices":["Use form and structure as the principal expression","Apply historical motifs to every surface","Hide the building's mass behind sculptural reliefs","Preserve ornament as an essential moral duty","Reject architectural function entirely"],"answer":"Use form and structure as the principal expression","why":"Loos argued for architecture expressed through its volumes and structure.","label":"Which approach to a plain building is most consistent with Adolf Loos's ","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-005","sourceQ":726,"stem":"The rooftop with sculptural chimney forms of Casa Milà belongs to which city?","choices":["Barcelona","Madrid","Valencia","Seville","Bilbao"],"answer":"Barcelona","why":"Casa Milà, or La Pedrera, is in Barcelona.","label":"The rooftop with sculptural chimney forms of Casa Milà belongs to which ","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-006","sourceQ":727,"stem":"The designer of the Cubo ashtray is also associated with experiments in visual communication. Who was he?","choices":["Bruno Munari","Enzo Mari","Ettore Sottsass","Marco Zanuso","Achille Castiglioni"],"answer":"Bruno Munari","why":"Bruno Munari designed Cubo and explored visual communication.","label":"The designer of the Cubo ashtray is also associated with experiments in ","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-007","sourceQ":728,"stem":"Which century contains the career of Piero della Francesca?","choices":["Fifteenth","Thirteenth","Fourteenth","Sixteenth","Seventeenth"],"answer":"Fifteenth","why":"Piero della Francesca lived from about 1412 to 1492, within the fifteenth century.","label":"Which century contains the career of Piero della Francesca","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-008","sourceQ":729,"stem":"A functional household object takes the form of a three-legged sculptural citrus press. Which designer made it?","choices":["Philippe Starck","Andrea Branzi","Enzo Mari","Marco Zanuso","Ron Arad"],"answer":"Philippe Starck","why":"Starck designed the Juicy Salif citrus press for Alessi.","label":"A functional household object takes the form of a three-legged sculptura","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-009","sourceQ":730,"stem":"Which style immediately preceded Mannerism in the usual survey of Italian art?","choices":["Renaissance","Romanesque","Gothic","Neoclassicism","Art Deco"],"answer":"Renaissance","why":"Mannerism developed from late Renaissance artistic practice.","label":"Which style immediately preceded Mannerism in the usual survey of Italia","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-010","sourceQ":731,"stem":"A church's long central aisle leads from the entrance toward the altar. What is this space called?","choices":["Nave","Transept","Ambulatory","Apse","Crypt"],"answer":"Nave","why":"The nave is the longitudinal central space of a church.","label":"A church's long central aisle leads from the entrance toward the altar. ","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-011","sourceQ":732,"stem":"Why did Monet paint Rouen Cathedral repeatedly at different times of day?","choices":["To compare the changing effect of light","To document its structural failure","To record successive reconstructions","To design a new façade","To imitate Roman frescoes"],"answer":"To compare the changing effect of light","why":"The series investigates how light and atmosphere change the façade's appearance.","label":"Why did Monet paint Rouen Cathedral repeatedly at different times of day","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-012","sourceQ":733,"stem":"In a Greek temple, what part lies immediately before the naos?","choices":["Pronaos","Peristyle","Opisthodomos","Stylobate","Pediment"],"answer":"Pronaos","why":"The pronaos is the entrance porch before the naos.","label":"In a Greek temple, what part lies immediately before the naos","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-013","sourceQ":734,"stem":"A work by Arman is titled Picassienne. Which artist is named in its title?","choices":["Pablo Picasso","Henri Matisse","Paul Cézanne","Edvard Munch","César Baldaccini"],"answer":"Pablo Picasso","why":"Picassienne references Pablo Picasso.","label":"A work by Arman is titled Picassienne. Which artist is named in its titl","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-014","sourceQ":736,"stem":"Which event predates the Spanish Civil War by three years?","choices":["Hitler's rise to power","The French Popular Front victory","The fall of the Berlin Wall","The Prague Spring","The Suez Crisis"],"answer":"Hitler's rise to power","why":"Hitler became German chancellor in 1933; the Spanish Civil War began in 1936.","label":"Which event predates the Spanish Civil War by three years","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-015","sourceQ":737,"stem":"Which Roman material made monolithic vaults and domes practical?","choices":["Opus caementicium","Bucchero","Tempera","Porphyry","Terracotta glaze"],"answer":"Opus caementicium","why":"Opus caementicium is a Roman concrete used in large vaulted construction.","label":"Which Roman material made monolithic vaults and domes practical","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-016","sourceQ":738,"stem":"A theatre cavea cut into a natural hillside is especially typical of which tradition?","choices":["Ancient Greek","Early Gothic","Baroque Italian","Industrial British","Etruscan funerary"],"answer":"Ancient Greek","why":"Greek theatres commonly used the hillside as support for seating.","label":"A theatre cavea cut into a natural hillside is especially typical of whi","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-017","sourceQ":739,"stem":"Carlo Alberto dalla Chiesa served as a general of which Italian force?","choices":["The Carabinieri","The Navy","The Guardia di Finanza","The Fire Brigade","The Air Force"],"answer":"The Carabinieri","why":"Dalla Chiesa was a Carabinieri general.","label":"Carlo Alberto dalla Chiesa served as a general of which Italian force","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-018","sourceQ":740,"stem":"Which category best describes Bakelite?","choices":["Synthetic polymer","Ceramic glaze","Natural stone","Animal fiber","Iron alloy"],"answer":"Synthetic polymer","why":"Bakelite is an early synthetic plastic, a thermosetting polymer.","label":"Which category best describes Bakelite","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-019","sourceQ":742,"stem":"Calling someone acqua e sapone most nearly suggests which quality?","choices":["Natural simplicity","Affected sophistication","Calculated cruelty","Miserliness","Indifference"],"answer":"Natural simplicity","why":"The idiom praises a natural and unpretentious manner.","label":"Calling someone acqua e sapone most nearly suggests which quality","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-020","sourceQ":743,"stem":"If a test pairs flamenco with Argentina, which correction makes the pair accurate?","choices":["Flamenco — Spain","Flamenco — Portugal","Flamenco — France","Flamenco — Mexico","Flamenco — Greece"],"answer":"Flamenco — Spain","why":"Flamenco is traditionally associated with Spain.","label":"If a test pairs flamenco with Argentina, which correction makes the pair","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-021","sourceQ":744,"stem":"Which of these palaces is in Vicenza?","choices":["Palazzo Chiericati","Palazzo Grassi","Palazzo Rosso","Palazzo Farnese","Palazzo Pandolfini"],"answer":"Palazzo Chiericati","why":"Palazzo Chiericati, designed by Palladio, stands in Vicenza.","label":"Which of these palaces is in Vicenza","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-022","sourceQ":745,"stem":"An architect's dynamic industrial-city drawings and a painter's studies of movement both belong to Italian Futurism. Which pair fits?","choices":["Sant'Elia and Boccioni","Palladio and Caravaggio","Loos and Monet","Alberti and Dalí","Bernini and Fontana"],"answer":"Sant'Elia and Boccioni","why":"Antonio Sant'Elia and Umberto Boccioni were associated with Futurism.","label":"An architect's dynamic industrial-city drawings and a painter's studies ","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-023","sourceQ":746,"stem":"Which architect designed New York's spiral Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum?","choices":["Frank Lloyd Wright","Louis Kahn","Walter Gropius","Le Corbusier","Renzo Piano"],"answer":"Frank Lloyd Wright","why":"Frank Lloyd Wright designed the Guggenheim Museum in New York.","label":"Which architect designed New York's spiral Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-024","sourceQ":748,"stem":"Which nineteenth-century novel is by the Russian writer Leo Tolstoy?","choices":["War and Peace","Madame Bovary","The Scarlet Letter","Jane Eyre","The Trial"],"answer":"War and Peace","why":"Tolstoy wrote War and Peace.","label":"Which nineteenth-century novel is by the Russian writer Leo Tolstoy","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-025","sourceQ":749,"stem":"The capture of Rome through Porta Pia occurred in which year?","choices":["1870","1848","1861","1915","1946"],"answer":"1870","why":"The breach at Porta Pia occurred on 20 September 1870.","label":"The capture of Rome through Porta Pia occurred in which year","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-026","sourceQ":750,"stem":"Which classical author wrote De architectura long before Renaissance treatise writers?","choices":["Vitruvius","Filarete","Alberti","Francesco di Giorgio Martini","Palladio"],"answer":"Vitruvius","why":"Vitruvius wrote De architectura in ancient Rome.","label":"Which classical author wrote De architectura long before Renaissance tre","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-027","sourceQ":751,"stem":"In which decade did the American Civil War begin?","choices":["1860s","1780s","1810s","1840s","1890s"],"answer":"1860s","why":"The American Civil War began in 1861.","label":"In which decade did the American Civil War begin","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-028","sourceQ":752,"stem":"The Greek military dictatorship known as the regime of the colonels began in which decade?","choices":["1960s","1920s","1940s","1980s","2000s"],"answer":"1960s","why":"The Greek junta seized power in 1967.","label":"The Greek military dictatorship known as the regime of the colonels bega","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-029","sourceQ":753,"stem":"Whose commercial competition was the English Navigation Act of 1651 especially intended to restrict?","choices":["Dutch shipping","Spanish merchants","Ottoman trade","French land transport","Portuguese plantations"],"answer":"Dutch shipping","why":"The act sought to curb Dutch dominance in carrying English trade.","label":"Whose commercial competition was the English Navigation Act of 1651 espe","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-030","sourceQ":754,"stem":"Which event in Italy preceded the armistice of September 1943?","choices":["Mussolini's arrest","The founding of the Salò Republic","The Fosse Ardeatine massacre","The fall of Rome to the Allies","The end of the war in Europe"],"answer":"Mussolini's arrest","why":"Mussolini was arrested on 25 July, before the September armistice.","label":"Which event in Italy preceded the armistice of September 1943","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-031","sourceQ":755,"stem":"At Actium, Octavian defeated a coalition led by Mark Antony and which Egyptian ruler?","choices":["Cleopatra VII","Hatshepsut","Nefertiti","Arsinoe II","Berenice IV"],"answer":"Cleopatra VII","why":"Cleopatra VII supported Mark Antony at Actium.","label":"At Actium, Octavian defeated a coalition led by Mark Antony and which Eg","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-032","sourceQ":756,"stem":"The word maniera, central to the name Mannerism, is best translated as what?","choices":["Manner or style","Structure","Volume","Perspective","Color"],"answer":"Manner or style","why":"The term refers to the style or manner of earlier masters.","label":"The word maniera, central to the name Mannerism, is best translated as w","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-033","sourceQ":757,"stem":"What diplomatic meeting redrew much of Europe after Napoleon's defeat?","choices":["Congress of Vienna","Congress of Berlin","Treaty of Utrecht","Yalta Conference","Peace of Westphalia"],"answer":"Congress of Vienna","why":"The Congress of Vienna concluded in 1815 after the Napoleonic wars.","label":"What diplomatic meeting redrew much of Europe after Napoleon's defeat","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-034","sourceQ":758,"stem":"Which vessel sank USS Housatonic during the American Civil War?","choices":["H. L. Hunley","HMS Dreadnought","USS Monitor","CSS Virginia","HMS Beagle"],"answer":"H. L. Hunley","why":"The submarine H. L. Hunley sank the Union warship in 1864.","label":"Which vessel sank USS Housatonic during the American Civil War","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-035","sourceQ":759,"stem":"A fresco classified as Pompeian Fourth Style belongs to a scheme with how many styles in total?","choices":["Four","Two","Three","Five","Six"],"answer":"Four","why":"The conventional Pompeian painting classification has four styles.","label":"A fresco classified as Pompeian Fourth Style belongs to a scheme with ho","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-036","sourceQ":760,"stem":"Where was the 1982 war between Argentina and the United Kingdom fought?","choices":["Falkland Islands","Cyprus","Malta","Azores","Canary Islands"],"answer":"Falkland Islands","why":"The conflict concerned the Falkland Islands, also called the Malvinas.","label":"Where was the 1982 war between Argentina and the United Kingdom fought","skill":"Adjacent concept · independently authored"},{"id":"NEWDER-037","sourceQ":761,"stem":"Which Catalan architect died in Barcelona in 1926?","choices":["Antoni Gaudí","Lluís Domè